    "title": "Rough weather early today",
    "text": "Downpours/scattered thunderstorms at times through the wee hours of the morning as a powerful storm system approaches. A Flood Watch and Wind Advisory is in effect through tonight for the entire state of Connecticut due to the expected combination of strong, damaging winds and periods of heavy rain. Local street, highway, basement, stream, and River Flooding are possible, along with Minor Coastal Flooding at times of high tide between 9 pm and midnight with large waves crashing onshore! Also, some Power Outages are likely. Mild, muggy, and foggy conditions too! Clearing and chilly for Tuesday, St. Patrick’s Day. Early this morning: Bands of heavy rain & possible thunderstorms with very gusty winds through coming through. Gusts 30-55MPH and isolated 60MPH causing some power outages. Mild 50s to low 60s and falling fast toward sunrise. Today (St Patrick’s Day): AM sun to more clouds for the afternoon, windy and turning colder with temperatures falling through the 40s into the 30s. Tomorrow: Mostly sunny and cold. Highs only in the upper 30s. Thursday: Some sun, chilly with highs in the mid 40s. Friday: Spring starts at 10:46 AM! Mostly sunny. More seasonable. Highs near 50. Saturday: Clouds increase with later day showers possible. High in the low-mid 50s. Sunday: Lots of clouds with more showers. Cooler. Highs in the mid 40s. Monday: Mostly sunny, windy and colder. Highs upper 30s. Tuesday: Mostly sunny and cool. Highs mid 40s.",
